## Screen 07 experiment

The third of five gold paddle meshes occupies the upper-left area of the approved frame. Its material permits the saved camera image to appear on the mesh near the approved viewing direction. The disposable test tightened only that mesh's angular blend. It retained Claudia's mesh, rounded bevels, texture objects, depth uniforms, camera, physics, and other four paddles.

The whole approved opening changed **zero pixels**. In equal-state forward travel, 11,075 pixels changed, but the image of a ring and purple slotted wall still crossed the paddle. Hard left changed 4,894 pixels and the same visual issue remained. On hard right, 14,474 pixels changed. The ring and wall slots lifted off the paddle face, revealing a broad, plain orange-gold slab with a simpler highlight. The early and sampled plunge views were identical. Each unchanged-material repeat at the seven paired poses had zero decoded pixel differences. Temporarily hiding the paddle in the disposable tab localized the effect to its silhouette. Hiding the two farther paddles also changed actual pixels, so a nearer tube ray hit by itself would have misidentified them as invisible.

**Reject the one-paddle material setting.** The hard-right view exposed a real correction opportunity, while forward and left travel retained the underlying image bleed. The hard-right replacement has flatter gold shading than the original art. The experiment's native frames include the full HUD, environment and character. Separate synchronized before and test clips show the same simulated camera, pose and input on every frame.

The next protected Screen 07 experiment should use a paddle-specific artwork mask to exclude wall perforations and ring stripes, retain the approved painted front face, and use Claudia's polished gold for the bevel and side. Study the real front and side from +10 forward and equal-distance hard turns. Any design choice for the unseen side needs owner review. The near-bank and plunge correction can continue on Claudia's own schedule.

Claudia's eight gameplay assertions passed both on the retained Screen 07 and with the one-paddle candidate installed. The full-game pickup run collected **91 coins** and went from **1,330 to 2,240**. This total comes from the gameplay regression run. Individual stage clips deliberately exercise steering and show their own live counters.

